# Byte-for-byte is this repository's unit of truth: the golden transcripts, the session bundles, the
# exported HTML/Markdown under tests/fixtures/ and the terminal-byte assertions are all compared as
# bytes, and `cargo fmt --check` compares sources the same way. A checkout that rewrote line endings
# would fail the suite for a reason that has nothing to do with the code — and that is precisely what
# a Windows runner does by default (`core.autocrlf=true` in its system gitconfig). So: no conversion,
# on any platform, for anything.
* -text
